The gate has three possible outputs (think of them as controls to the motor for the gate arm): ’raise’, ’lower’, and ’nop’. (Nop means “no operation.”)
Roughly, here is what the gate needs to do:
• If a car wants to come through, the gate needs to raise the arm until it is at the top position. • Once the gate is at the top position, it has to stay there until the car has driven through the gate. • After the car has driven through the gate needs to lower the arm until it reaches the bottom position.
